Polysite: third-party notices
=============================

Polysite itself is distributed under the terms in LICENSE.md. It includes, bundles or runs with the third-party software and
fonts listed here, each under its own licence. This file is generated and kept by hand in part: the sections below up to the
long lists are written by people, the lists are produced by a generator script that the maintainers keep privately from the lockfiles of apps/cms and apps/web
(production dependencies only; development tools are not shipped).

1. Fonts bundled in this repository (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
---------------------------------------------------------------
  Lora         Copyright 2011 The Lora Project Authors (https://github.com/cyrealtype/Lora-Cyrillic),
               with Reserved Font Name "Lora".
  Inter        Copyright 2016 The Inter Project Authors (https://github.com/rsms/inter).

Only the Latin subset at weight 600 is included, as a woff2 file, taken unchanged from the npm packages @fontsource/lora 5.2.8
and @fontsource/inter 5.2.8 (which publish the files served by Google Fonts). Where they are:

  apps/cms/public/fonts/    lora-latin-600-normal.woff2, inter-latin-600-normal.woff2   (the admin)
  apps/web/public/fonts/    lora-latin-600-normal.woff2                                  (the public error page)

The licence text sits next to the files (OFL-Lora.txt, OFL-Inter.txt) and must stay with them. The OFL allows bundling and
redistributing the fonts with software; they may not be sold on their own. Lora declares a Reserved Font Name: the files are used
as published, without changes, so the name is kept; if they are ever modified (re-subsetted, converted), check the OFL first.

2. Components with licence terms that deserve a note
----------------------------------------------------
  libvips (LGPL-3.0-or-later). The packages @img/sharp-libvips-* hold the prebuilt libvips shared library that "sharp"
      (Apache-2.0) loads to resize images and convert them to WebP in the CMS (and that the public site's image tooling also
      installs). It is not modified and is not linked into Polysite's own code: it is a separate library that sharp loads at
      run time and that can be replaced by installing another build. Source and build scripts: https://github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips
      and https://github.com/libvips/libvips. LGPL text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html
  lightningcss (MPL-2.0), used by the public site's build to process CSS, with its platform packages (lightningcss-*). Not
      modified. MPL-2.0 is a file-level licence; its source is at https://github.com/parcel-bundler/lightningcss and the licence
      text at https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
  dompurify (MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0): used under Apache-2.0.
  node-forge ((BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0)): used under BSD-3-Clause.
  caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0): browser-support data, by Alexis Deveria and contributors (https://github.com/browserslist/caniuse-lite).
  argparse (Python-2.0), sanitize-filename, truncate-utf8-bytes and utf8-byte-length (WTFPL, some dual-licensed), and a few
