3. Docker images
----------------
The images are built on node:24-alpine (Node.js, MIT; Alpine Linux packages carry their own licences), and the stack runs
caddy:2-alpine (Apache-2.0), postgres:16-alpine (PostgreSQL Licence) and redis:7-alpine (BSD-3-Clause for the 7.x line: pin the
version deliberately, later Redis releases changed licence). The backup image adds rclone (MIT), OpenSSL (Apache-2.0), curl (curl licence)
and tzdata (public domain) to the Postgres image. None of these is part of this repository, and they are not listed below.

4. Optional repositories
------------------------
The plugins (polysite-plugins) and themes (polysite-themes) are separate repositories with their own NOTICE files.

5. For the lawyer
-----------------
Open points: the LGPL libvips and MPL lightningcss notes above (dynamic use, unmodified); the Lora Reserved Font Name; the
vaul-vue licence; and development-only tools, which were not scanned.

